  "body": {
    "id": "lem:sc-profiled-normal-rank",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "At every \\(P_0\\in\\mathcal M_I\\) such that, for every \\(x\\in\\mathcal X\\) and \\(1\\le g\\le J+1\\), \\(p_X(x)>\\kappa_0\\), \\(p_g(x)\\in(\\epsilon_0,1-\\epsilon_0)\\), \\(\\max_{g,t}E_{P_{0,O}}[|Y_t|^4\\mid G=g]<M_4\\), \\(\\lambda_{\\min}\\{B(x)^{\\prime}B(x)\\}>\\kappa_0\\), every nonzero eigenvalue of \\(\\Omega_x\\) is greater than \\(\\kappa_0\\), and \\(\\operatorname{rank}(\\Omega_x)\\) is locally constant, the derivative of the profiled SC restriction in stratum \\(x\\) is \\[\\dot r_{\\mathrm{SC},x}=\\{I_T-B(x)[B(x)^{\\prime}B(x)]^{-1}B(x)^{\\prime}\\}\\{\\dot a(x)-\\dot B(x)w(x)\\}.\\] Consequently, \\[\\operatorname{rank}E_{P_{0,O}}[R_{\\mathrm{SC},x}R_{\\mathrm{SC},x}^{\\prime}]\\le T-J.\\] Equality holds when the covariance form of the residualized coordinates is positive definite on the \\((T-J)\\)-dimensional orthogonal complement of \\(\\operatorname{col}B(x)\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "P0",
      "PO",
      "MI",
