    ],
    "proof_tex": "Fix a stratum \\(x\\) at the strict-interior, locally constant-rank point in the statement and put \\(\\Pi_x=B(x)\\{B(x)^{\\prime}B(x)\\}^{-1}B(x)^{\\prime}\\).  The strict SC Gram margin makes \\(\\Pi_x\\) the orthogonal projector onto the \\(J\\)-dimensional column space of \\(B(x)\\), so \\(I_T-\\Pi_x\\) has rank \\(T-J\\).  At an SC law, \\(a(x)=B(x)w(x)\\).  Differentiating \\(\\Pi_xB(x)=B(x)\\) yields\n\\[\n \\dot\\Pi_xB(x)w(x)=(I_T-\\Pi_x)\\dot B(x)w(x).\n \\tag{1}\n\\]\nSince \\(r_{\\mathrm{SC},x}=(I_T-\\Pi_x)a(x)\\),\n\\[\n \\dot r_{\\mathrm{SC},x}\n =(I_T-\\Pi_x)\\{\\dot a(x)-\\dot B(x)w(x)\\}.\n \\tag{2}\n\\]\nThe definition of \\(R_{\\mathrm{SC},x}\\) uses the conditional-residual Riesz representative of exactly this derivative.  Conditional centering does not change the deterministic range in (2).  Thus the covariance range of \\(R_{\\mathrm{SC},x}\\) is contained in \\(\\operatorname{range}(I_T-\\Pi_x)\\), proving the rank bound \\(T-J\\).  If the residualized covariance form is positive definite on that range, its covariance rank equals the range dimension, proving equality.",
    "justification": "The lemma certifies the finite SC normal dimension at the same strict-interior constant-rank points as the envelope.",
    "gap": "The profiled derivative and its exact residual-space rank are needed for the QP geometry.",
    "consumer": "This is a rank calculation, not an inference guarantee.",
